<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AWB Australian wheat indicator prices-Nov 15.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AWB Australian wheat indicator prices-Nov 15.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>International prices for milling wheat were weaker. With no significant export business and the recent runup in prices world wheat values simply traded lower, the Austalian Wheat Board (AWB) said. Wheat indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1996/97 crop wheat fell A$2.00 (Duram prices not applicable). Prices, FOB, A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		    ASW 10 pct		   No 1 DURUM</p>
<p>		    Delivered Port	     Delivered Port</p>
<p>Queensland</p>
<p>    Brisbane	n/a</p>
<p>    Gladstone     n/a</p>
<p>    Mackay	  n/a</p>
<p>New South Wales</p>
<p>    Newcastle     132.75			   n/a</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   133.75</p>
<p>Victoria</p>
<p>    Geelong	 134.00</p>
<p>    Portland	134.75</p>
<p>South Australia</p>
<p>    Port Adelaide 134.75			   n/a</p>
<p>    Port Giles    135.50</p>
<p>Port Lincoln  137.00</p>
<p>    Port Pirie    131.50</p>
<p>    Thevenard     132.00</p>
<p>    Wallaroo	133.25</p>
<p>Western Australia</p>
<p>    Albany	  140.25</p>
<p>    Esperance     138.75</p>
<p>    Fremantle     143.00</p>
<p>    Geraldton     140.00</p>
<p>NOTE: The indicator price represents the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract price offered today by the AWB for wheat delivered during the 1996/97 harvest. The offer is valid until 4.30 p.m. Australian Eastern Standard Summer Time (0530 GMT).</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
